# rpcbind FHS migration: state dir and lock /run/* -> /var/run/*.
#
# --with-statedir=/var/run/rpcbind moves the warm-start state dir
# (configure knob). The lock file RPCBINDDLOCK is hardcoded upstream
# with no knob, so files/rpcbind-run-lock.patch moves it to the flat
# /var/run/rpcbind.lock (upstream flat shape preserved).
#
# Stale-state policy (/var/run is persistent by design, never wiped):
# - Liveness is lock-validated by the daemon itself (open + err on
#   a live lock, unlink on clean exit). The OpenRC pidfile is
#   tracking-only. No pid/lock cleanup in service logic.
# - New /var/run/rpcbind: converged here on upgrade (root-owned
#   0755; root-run suite, no accounts.d identity); created by
#   checkpath (OpenRC) and ExecStartPre (systemd, root unit).
# - Old /run/rpcbind: volatile residue on tmpfs. Removed once
#   empty; left in place and reported while the old daemon runs.
#   The old flat /run/rpcbind.pid was tracking-only tmpfs residue
#   needing no migration.

dir /var/run/rpcbind 0755 root root
rmdir-if-empty /run/rpcbind
